h injured his knee in the second round and had to withdraw.  This left Ryan unchallenged and he won easily. Ryan did not approach his own world record of 57.77 (set in 1913), nor did he challenge McGrath’s Olympic record of 54.74. All qualifying marks were carried over to the final round."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Some sources state that " [:a {:href "/athletes/69346"} "Tom Nicolson"] " arrived late and did not compete in the qualifying, and a petition by the other contestants allowed him to compete in the finals. " [:em {} "Gazet van Antwerpen"] " states that Nicolson qualified for the final by throwing in a special trial later in the afternoon. Thus, it would seem that there were seven athletes advanced to the final, instead of the original six, as the rules stated. Although " [:a {:href "/athletes/76267"} "Nils Linde"] " was then seventh in qualifying, he did compete in the final, per " [:em {} "Dalpilen"] ", a Falun (SWE) newspaper. Eventually, only six athletes competed in the final, as McGrath withdrew after injuring his knee. His qualifying mark was carried over to the final, which allowed him to place fifth."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Qualifying"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "229"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/78986"} "Paddy Ryan"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "52.830 (1)"] [:td {} "52.875 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {:class "bib"} "599"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/76257"} "Carl Johan Lind"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/SWE"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-c